<title>UK: UK's Ultra wins contract from Bombardier.</title>
<headline>UK's Ultra wins contract from Bombardier.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Ultra Electronics Holdings Plc said on Monday it will supply Active Noise and Vibration Control equipment to Canadair, a unit of Canada's Bombardier Aerospace.</p>
<p>The defence and aerospace manufacturer said the contract was to supply the system, which reduces turbofan noise inside the cabin of the Challenger business jet, for both new Challenger 604 aircraft and for retrofit to Challenger 601 and early Challenger 604 aircraft.</p>
<p>It did not disclose any financial details.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
